                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the inpatient treatment of your 77-year-old patient, admitted on 08/07/2025 due to acutely decompensated chronic congestive heart failure. On admission, clinical examination revealed marked peripheral oedema, pulmonary congestion, and reduced exercise tolerance. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray confirming pulmonary congestion, ECG, echocardiography demonstrating reduced left ventricular function, and laboratory investigations. Oxygen saturation was monitored continuously. Treatment consisted of intravenous diuresis with furosemide, resulting in significant fluid mobilisation, alongside optimisation of oral heart failure medication including ACE inhibitor, beta-blocker, and aldosterone antagonist. The patient responded well to therapy with clear clinical improvement. Urinary output was monitored via indwelling catheter. He was discharged on 16/07/2025 in stable condition. Please continue outpatient follow-up and monitor renal function and electrolytes closely. I remain at your disposal for any queries.</div>"
            },
